<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cunigunde of Luxembourg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 975–<a href="/years/1040">1040</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Saint Cunigunde</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cunigunde of Luxembourg was the wife of Emperor Henry II and was crowned empress in 1014. She acted as regent after his death in 1024 and then retired to the convent of Kaufungen, which she had founded. Venerated for her piety, she was canonised in 1200 and is buried beside Henry in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamberg">Bamberg</a> Cathedral.</p></div>
